Falsifies `byte_glob::verification::star_matches_anything_and_question_matches_one_byte`.

The defect: once the name is spent, the matcher skips `?` as well as `*`, so `?` matches the empty name.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert_eq!(matches_with(b"?", n, Dot::Ordinary), nlen == 1)` at `nlen == 0`.

